==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|anthropo-|-centric}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Placing [[human]]s at the center of something, giving preference to humans above all other considerations.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=w:The Omnivore's Dilemma|author=w:Michael Pollan|publisher=The Penguin Press|year=2006|ISBN=1594200823|passage=But just as we recognize that nature doesn't provide a very good guide for human social conduct, isn't it '''anthropocentric''' of us to assume that our moral system offers an adequate guide for what should happen in nature?|page=325}}

